{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>All the days of the earth.</b> The covenant is cut only until the heavens vanish like smoke and the earth wear out like a garment." "<b>Seed and harvest and cold and heat.</b> Half of Kislev, Tevet, and half of Shevat — winter, etc., in Bava Metzia. This is what is stated in Bava Metzia, chapter HaMekabel: half of Tishrei, Marcheshvan, and half of Kislev — seed; half of Kislev, Tevet, and half of Shevat — cold; half of Shevat, Adar, and half of Nisan — cold; half of Nisan, Iyyar, and half of Sivan — harvest; half of Sivan, Tammuz, and half of Av — summer; half of Av, Elul, and half of Tishrei — heat." "<b>[Shall not cease.</b> They shall not cease.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The lemma lists four pairs (seed/harvest, cold/heat) but the six-season scheme from Bava Metzia (BK 106b) yields six items; the alignment of חורף with קור in the biblical verse is implicit. The first two lines before חז״ק are a shorthand citation; the full source passage follows."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:35.391147942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}